        ecrm:P3_has_note    "Scarf made of brocaded silk. The scarf is of white tabby with a ribbed 0.5 inch wide selvedge, with ribbing repeated as an end feature at either end of the scarf. Above this is a meandering band of small six-petalled flowers brocaded in pink silk with green centres on a stem of white leaves formed by the weft bound in fancy twills by a portion of the warp, and the remainder floats on the back. Above this band are three brocaded sprays of small pink flowers in a cluster of green leaves. Above these are two smaller similar sprays."@en ;
